      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:5:3:34:2",
      "text": [
        " تَزَوَّجِ الْحُرَّةَ عَلَى الْأَمَةِ وَ لَا تَزَوَّجِ الْأَمَةَ عَلَى الْحُرَّةِ وَ مَنْ تَزَوَّجَ أَمَةً عَلَى حُرَّةٍ فَنِكَاحُهُ بَاطِلٌ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Ali Bin Ibrahim, from his father, from Ibn Abu Umeyr, from Hammad, from Al halby, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> having said: ‘You can marry the free woman upon the slave girl (as an additional wife), but you cannot marry the slave girl (as an additional wife) upon the free woman; and the one who marries the slave girl (as an additional wife) upon a free woman, so his marriage is void’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "2. Ali ibn Ibrahim has narrated from his father from ibn abu ‘Umayr from Hammad from al-Halabiy who has said the following: “Abu ’Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, has said, ‘A free woman can become a second wife, the first wife being a slave-girl; but a slave-girl cannot become a second wife, the first wife being a free woman. If one marries a slave-girl as a second wife, the first being a free woman, such marriage is invalid.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
